Decision: route every macOS Agent shell through the existing pre-Tauri helper, remove process-injection variables, and let an external guard kill only its exact process group when Beaver dies.
Reason: Beaver's in-process macOS watchdog disappears in a SIGBUS crash, while allowing loader injection into the guard would bypass its checks before the full-disk shell starts.
